<title>USA: U.S. ITC to continue Chile salmon dumping probe.</title>
<headline>U.S. ITC to continue Chile salmon dumping probe.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. International Trade Commission voted three to zero on Thursday to continue its probe into accusations Chile has been dumping salmon on the U.S. market.</p>
<p>&quot;There is a reasonable indication that a U.S. industry is materially injured by reason of imports of fresh Atlantic salmon from Chile that are allegedly subsidized and sold in the United States at less than fair value,&quot; the ITC said in a statement.</p>
</text>
